# grape-heif.exe: Rust crates

`grape-heif.exe` is Grape's HEIC helper on Windows (DECISIONS D33). It's a separate program, GPL-3.0-or-later as a whole because of the C libraries it links (see `LICENSE.txt`, `libheif.txt`, `libde265.txt`, `libde265-win32cond.txt`, `x265.txt` and `SOURCE.md` in this folder). This file lists the Rust crates compiled into it:

- **{{len @root.crates}} Rust crates**, grouped by license. Each license's full text follows the crates that use it.

When a crate offers a choice of licenses, Grape takes MIT where it can.

This file is generated by cargo-about from `tools/grape-heif/Cargo.lock`, `tools/grape-heif/about.toml` and `tools/grape-heif/about.hbs`, so don't edit it by hand. Regenerate it from the repo root:

```
cargo about generate --locked --fail --manifest-path tools/grape-heif/Cargo.toml -c tools/grape-heif/about.toml -o licenses/grape-heif/rust-crates.md tools/grape-heif/about.hbs
```

